{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794129977,"nonce":"C+VOhIsQXKGCq6QQcolKtiKegwI=","message":"Correction to my survey comment: I said the theme's list would resolve DejaVu Sans on Omarchy while the registry resolves Noto Sans. That is wrong. The CSS family parser keeps only the first named family and the first generic keyword, so the theme's other fallbacks never reach the registry; a missing first name falls to the system face, which is the registry's list. Effective order is the theme's first name, then the registry list, then fontdb's generic sans. So the lists did not disagree in practice on Omarchy; what was wrong is that Adwaita Sans was in neither list, Cantarell was named first, and the theme's extra entries were inert and misleading. Done in the working tree: one shared list, blinc_core::system_fonts::LINUX_SANS (Adwaita Sans, Cantarell, Ubuntu, Noto Sans, DejaVu Sans), read by the registry's Linux default and by the Linux theme. Tests on the Ubuntu NUC: the theme names the shared list in both schemes, the registry's list is the shared list, and with the first families missing (Adwaita Sans, Cantarell are not installed there) the system face is the first installed one. The fontconfig-first option stays open.","files":null}]}